Reply with only one JSON object, shaped exactly like this example:
{% if kind == "species" -%}
{"name": "...", "lifespan": 0, "adult_age": 0, "measures": [{"name": "height", "min": 0, "max": 0, "unit": "ft"}], "aka": [{"name": "...", "tag": "common", "everyday": true}], "facts": [{"category": "origin", "text": "One claim, in a full sentence."}, {"category": "general", "text": "Another claim."}], "names": [{"name": "...", "kind": "place", "aka": []}]}

- "name": the species' name.{% if has_name %} Use the name already decided: "{{ name }}".{% else %} Invent one if the prompt doesn't give it.{% endif %}
- "lifespan": how long they typically live, in years, as a number.
- "adult_age": the age in years at which they are grown, as a number.
- "measures": their typical body ranges, each {"name", "min", "max", "unit"} with min and max as numbers: always height, plus any other measure that matters for this body (wingspan, tail length, tusk length...).
- The 0s in the example are placeholders: give real numbers that fit this species and the owner's prompt.
- "facts": between {{ min_facts }} and {{ max_facts }} facts, one claim each. "category" is one of: {{ categories | join(", ") }}. physical: the body; instinct: inborn tendencies; variation: how members differ from each other; origin: where they come from.
- Leave "since" out: these facts describe the species for as long as it has existed, and are never dated.
{%- elif kind == "race" -%}
{"name": "...", "measures": [{"name": "{{ example_measure }}", "min": 0, "max": 0, "unit": "ft"}], "aka": [{"name": "...", "tag": "common", "everyday": true}], "facts": [{"category": "physical", "text": "One claim, in a full sentence."}, {"category": "variation", "text": "Another claim."}], "no_longer_true": [], "names": [{"name": "...", "kind": "place", "aka": []}]}

- "name": the race's name.{% if has_name %} Use the name already decided: "{{ name }}".{% else %} Use the prompt's name if it gives one.{% endif %}
- "lifespan", "adult_age" and "measures": give each only where this race differs from {{ species_name }} (a measure narrower or outside the species' range); leave out any that is the same, it is inherited. lifespan and adult_age are years, as numbers; each measure is {"name", "min", "max", "unit"}, using the species' measure names.
- The 0s in the example are placeholders: give real numbers that fit this race and the owner's prompt.
- "facts": between 4 and 8 facts, one claim each, only what is specific to this race. "category" is one of: {{ categories | join(", ") }}.
- "no_longer_true": after the facts, the labels of the species facts that are untrue for this race now that your facts hold, such as ["F4"]. An inherited fact your facts only add detail to stays true and isn't listed; an empty list is fine when nothing changes.
- Leave "since" out: these facts describe the race for as long as it has existed, and are never dated.
{%- elif heritage_label -%}
{"name": "...", "age": 34, "aka": [{"name": "...", "tag": "common", "everyday": true}], "facts": [{"category": "{{ categories[0] }}", "text": "One claim, in a full sentence.", "overrides": []}, {"category": "background", "text": "Another claim.", "since": "YEAR"}], "names": [{"name": "...", "kind": "place", "aka": []}]{% if spheres %}, "ties": [{"sphere": "...", "role": "practitioner", "since": "YEAR", "exceptions": [{"text": "One sentence.", "rejects": "S1"}]}]{% endif %}}

- "name": the character's name.{% if has_name %} Use the name already decided.{% else %} Invent one if the prompt doesn't give it.{% endif %}
- "age": how old the character is now, in years, as a number.
- "facts": between {{ min_facts }} and {{ max_facts }} facts, one claim each. "category" is one of: {{ categories | join(", ") }}.
- "overrides": the labels of the inherited facts this fact makes untrue for this character, such as ["F4"]. Use it only for a real contradiction: if an inherited fact says "grey fur" and this character has black fur, the black-fur fact overrides it. A fact that adds detail to an inherited fact, builds on it or simply fits with it overrides nothing: "scarred paws" fits "padded paws", so no label. Most facts have an empty list; a reply usually overrides between none and two inherited facts.
- "since" is optional. Give it only when a fact started at a known time, and only as a year of this calendar, as a bare number no later than {{ now_year }}; "YEAR" in the example stands for that number. Leave it out otherwise: never a phrase like "childhood" or "ten years ago".
- Leave "since" out for an inherent trait that has always been true -- a species, the appearance someone is born with, a lifelong temperament -- rather than dating it to the present year.
{%- else -%}
{"name": "...", {% if kind == "character" %}"age": 34, {% endif %}"aka": [{"name": "...", "tag": "common", "everyday": true}], "facts": [{"category": "{{ categories[0] }}", "text": "One claim, in a full sentence.", "since": "YEAR"{% if nearby %}, "held_by": null{% endif %}}, {"category": "{{ categories[-1] }}", "text": "Another claim."{% if nearby %}, "held_by": null{% endif %}}], "names": [{"name": "...", "kind": "place", "aka": []}]{% if nearby %}, "elsewhere": [{"entry": "<an entry's name>", "text": "A claim mainly about that entry, in a full sentence.", "held_by": null}]{% endif %}{% if broader %}, "move_in": ["<an M label>"]{% endif %}{% if spheres %}, "ties": [{"sphere": "...", "role": "practitioner", "since": "YEAR", "exceptions": [{"text": "One sentence.", "rejects": "S1"}]}]{% endif %}}

- "name": the {{ kind }}'s name.{% if has_name %} Use the name already decided.{% else %} Invent one if the prompt doesn't give it.{% endif %}
{% if kind == "character" -%}
- "age": how old the character is now, in years, as a number.
{% endif -%}
- "facts": between {{ min_facts }} and {{ max_facts }} facts, one claim each. "category" is one of: {{ categories | join(", ") }}.
- "since" is optional. Give it only when a fact started at a known time, and only as a year of this calendar, as a bare number no later than {{ now_year }}; "YEAR" in the example stands for that number. Leave it out otherwise: never a phrase like "childhood" or "ten years ago".
- Leave "since" out for an inherent trait that has always been true -- a species, the appearance someone is born with, a lifelong temperament -- rather than dating it to the present year.
{%- endif %}
- "aka": other names for this {{ kind }} itself, if it has any, each {"name", "tag", "everyday"}. "tag" is "proper" for another formal name, or "common" for what people in the world actually call it day to day (a short form, a nickname). Set "everyday" true on the one common name people use most, false on the rest. "name" stays the most formal name. An empty list is fine.
- "names": after the facts, every proper name your facts use, other than this {{ kind }}'s own: people, places, peoples and species, named events, named groups and named objects, new or already in the world. Each is {"name", "kind", "aka"}: "name" in full, as your facts write it; "kind" one of character, place, species, race, sphere, event, item, lore; "aka" any other names your facts use for the same thing. A faith or church, an order, academy, guild or council, a culture, or a field of knowledge or magic is "sphere", with a "template": religion, order, culture or field, only these (a country or realm is a place; a rank or office is lore; so is any other group or faction, and a law, code, script or language). Proper names only: never a description such as "the postmaster", "a war" or "his mother", nor a title on its own such as "the Tsar" or "the High Bishop", nor a people's adjective such as "Moscavian" on its own -- but "Yelena" in "his mother Yelena" is a name. An empty list is fine.
{%- if nearby %}
- Keep "facts" to claims mainly about the {{ kind }} itself: a claim mainly about another entry goes in "elsewhere".
- "elsewhere": after the names, what you would add about other entries, each {"entry", "text", "held_by"}: "entry" the entry's name as the list of entries near this one writes it, or a new name you also list in "names"; "text" one claim in a full sentence. Never the {{ kind }} itself. An empty list is fine.
- A claim that ties another entry to the {{ kind }} ("it is taught at X", "unlike X, it...", "X uses it") is the {{ kind }}'s own: it goes in "facts". "elsewhere" is only for what another entry's page should say even if the {{ kind }} didn't exist.
{%- endif %}
{%- if broader %}
- "move_in": the labels of {{ broader_name }}'s facts above that are mainly about this {{ kind }}, so they belong on its page rather than on {{ broader_name }}'s. They move here: don't write them again in "facts". A fact that only mentions the {{ kind }} in passing stays where it is. An empty list is fine.
{%- endif %}
{%- if spheres %}
- "ties": after the names, the spheres above this character belongs to, each {"sphere", "role", "since", "exceptions"}: "sphere" its name as written above; "role" a word or two for how they belong (practitioner, priest, elder, scholar, member); "since" the year they joined, as a bare number no later than {{ now_year }}, or left out. Only the spheres above: never invent one here. An empty list is fine.
- "exceptions": only where this character departs from the sphere, each {"text", "rejects"}: "text" one sentence on what they reject or do differently, and "rejects" the label of the item it departs from, such as "S3". The character already holds everything else the sphere holds, so never restate it, in an exception or in the facts. Most ties have no exception or one.
- Write each exception only there, never again as one of the facts.
{%- endif %}

No commentary, no markdown fences, just the JSON object.
